# =============================================================================
#  All three images (api, migrations, web) build with the repository root as
#  their context, so this is the single ignore file for the whole repo. Keeping
#  one context is deliberate: Central Package Management puts
#  Directory.Packages.props and global.json at the root, and restore inside the
#  container fails without them.
#
#  Two entries here are correctness, not speed:
#    - **/node_modules  a host node_modules is built for Windows and would
#                       shadow the Linux one `npm ci` installs in the image.
#    - **/bin, **/obj   host build output leaks stale assets and NuGet
#                       assets files into the SDK stage.
# =============================================================================

# --- VCS and tooling ---------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.claude
.vs
.idea
.vscode
**/*.user
**/*.suo

# --- .NET build output -------------------------------------------------------
artifacts
**/bin
**/obj

# --- Node --------------------------------------------------------------------
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.vite
**/npm-debug.log*

# --- Not needed to build any image -------------------------------------------
tests
infra
docs
**/*.md
**/*.docx
**/*.zip
UI for project review
db
StockPortfolio.slnx
**/*.http

# --- Docker / env ------------------------------------------------------------
docker-compose*.yml
# Only real secrets. src/Web/.env* is left alone on purpose - Vite reads
# .env.production at build time and excluding it would silently change the
# bundle's configuration.
.env
.env.local
**/.env.local
